#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:1
msgid "Release 1.11 (2016-01-19)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:3
msgid ""
"This is primarily a bug fix release. It also has a number of new features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:6
msgid ""
"`nix-prefetch-url` can now download URLs specified in a Nix expression. For "
"example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:11
msgid ""
"will prefetch the file specified by the `fetchurl` call in the attribute "
"`hello.src` from the Nix expression in the current directory, and print the "
"cryptographic hash of the resulting file on stdout. This differs from `nix-"
"build -A                 hello.src` in that it doesn't verify the hash, and "
"is thus useful when you’re updating a Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:18
msgid ""
"You can also prefetch the result of functions that unpack a tarball, such as "
"`fetchFromGitHub`. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:21
msgid ""
"    $ nix-prefetch-url --unpack https://github.com/NixOS/patchelf/"
"archive/0.8.tar.gz\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:23
msgid "or from a Nix expression:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:27
msgid ""
"The builtin function `<nix/fetchurl.nix>` now supports downloading and "
"unpacking NARs. This removes the need to have multiple downloads in the "
"Nixpkgs stdenv bootstrap process (like a separate busybox binary for Linux, "
"or curl/mkdir/sh/bzip2 for Darwin). Now all those files can be combined into "
"a single NAR, optionally compressed using `xz`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:34
msgid ""
"Nix now supports SHA-512 hashes for verifying fixed-output derivations, and "
"in `builtins.hashString`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:37
msgid ""
"The new flag `--option build-repeat                         N` will cause "
"every build to be executed _N_+1 times. If the build output differs between "
"any round, the build is rejected, and the output paths are not registered as "
"valid. This is primarily useful to verify build determinism. (We already had "
"a `--check` option to repeat a previously succeeded build. However, with `--"
"check`, non-deterministic builds are registered in the DB. Preventing that "
"is useful for Hydra to ensure that non-deterministic builds don't end up "
"getting published to the binary cache.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:47
msgid ""
"The options `--check` and `--option                         build-repeat N`, "
"if they detect a difference between two runs of the same derivation and `-K` "
"is given, will make the output of the other run available under `store-path-"
"check`. This makes it easier to investigate the non-determinism using tools "
"like `diffoscope`, e.g.,"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:68
msgid "Improved FreeBSD support."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:70
msgid "`nix-env -qa --xml --meta` now prints license information."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:72
msgid ""
"The maximum number of parallel TCP connections that the binary cache "
"substituter will use has been decreased from 150 to 25. This should prevent "
"upsetting some broken NAT routers, and also improves performance."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:77
msgid ""
"All \"chroot\"-containing strings got renamed to \"sandbox\". In particular, "
"some Nix options got renamed, but the old names are still accepted as lower-"
"priority aliases."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:81
msgid ""
